<article class="env-lemma" id="06NS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06NS">Lemma <span data-tag="06NS">8.8.5</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $\mathcal{X}$ be a fibred category over $\mathcal{C}$. The stackification of the inertia fibred category $\mathcal{I}_\mathcal {X}$ is inertia of the stackification of $\mathcal{X}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from the fact that stackification is compatible with $2$-fibre products by Lemma <a href="/tag/04Y1" data-tag="04Y1">8.8.4</a> and the fact that there is a formula for the inertia in terms of $2$-fibre products of categories over $\mathcal{C}$, see Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/034H" data-tag="034H">4.34.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>